      "sequence_position": 7,
      "problem": "Consider the following sequence: \n\n$$\n5,\\,1,\\,-3,\\,-7,\\,-11,\\,…\n$$\n\nThe recursive formula for this sequence is given by \n\n${a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}, \n$\\,{a}_{1}=$ \n{{field-2}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that the first term of the sequence is ${a}_{1}=5.$\n\nInspecting the terms of the sequence, we see that we always get the next term by subtracting $4.$\n\nTherefore, the recursive rule must be the following:\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}-4\\,,\\,{a}_{1}=5\n$$",
